{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/391536-playtesting-wraith-20-argos","id":391536,"title":"Playtesting Wraith 20 Argos","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-03T09:31:23-08:00","id":391536,"title":"Playtesting Wraith 20 Argos","content":"My group found so far that the new system for Phantom Wings needs to be reviewed. Spending one Pathos and then rolling creates the possible scenario where the roll achieves no success (it happened twice so far), and hence the power fails. But it still cost one Pathos.<br /> Also, is really the design of the power for the flight to be of such a short duration? One turn per success is almost nothing, and it means that Wraith can't fly around, rather, they can only fly in emergencies. Even in the Tempest they can't fly continuously. <br /> <br /> We are trying with this house rule: one Pathos to manifest the wings. It lasts for a scene or one journey. Rolls are only to maneuver or carry passengers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T16:14:45-08:00","id":392008,"title":"","content":"I might ask my current Argos possessing player to try these out. Though, as I go through the PDF I notice that &quot;Jump&quot; is no longer listed. I wonder if its just been outright removed or will appear in some other form.... ...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T20:43:35-08:00","id":394408,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Ever since the Arcanoi previews for Wr20, I\u2019ve been messing around with Argos tweaks, just to give it a bit more oomph.<br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Tweak One</span></b><br /> Much like you, I nixed the \u2018turn per success\u2019 for Phantom Wings<br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Tweak Two</span></b><br /> Mattel Apes Deuce (or whatever), Argos 5, is cool and entirely appropriate for the Art. However, to even use it, a character needs to be in control of a Relic/Artifact vehicle. IIRC, that\u2019s a three-dot something (at least) just to use a power. Its mechanics don\u2019t change, but it slides down to Argos 4.<br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Tweak Three</span></b><br /> Tempest-Rider\u2019s Canceleer (Argos 4) is really cool! In terms of crunch and fluff, I love it. The cost and level make it a smidge underwhelming. Instead, slide this gem up the vacant Argos 5 (Ancient) slot. Keep the cost and powers the same, but \u2013 like Phantom Wings \u2013 remove the \u2018turn-per-success;\u2019 it lasts the scene.<br /> <br /> Try 'em out and tell me what you think. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T23:57:12-08:00","id":395899,"title":"","content":"The one turn per success rule has always been part of Phantom Wings, they are Wraiths not Angels after all, it's meant to be a kind of emergency option of movement not something you can do all the time, which is what will happen if it cost one Pathos and lasts a Scene.<br /> <br /> Just saying...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T10:45:38-08:00","id":399009,"title":"","content":"@Possessed<br /> <br /> The idea that the design of the power is meant for it to be used only in emergencies occurred to me.<br /> <br /> But in actual play i've been feeling that travel is a very big narrative concern for wraith games. It is very difficult. A wraith needs to travel through the tempest, not always safe, or walk very long distances. Allowing players to fly around so far has brought no troubles, instead it has enhanced the flow of my games.<br /> <br /> And tempest travelling in the books mentions flying so often, it is hard to picture this being done only a few turns every once and a while.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> @nazfool<br /> <br /> Thanks for the input.<br /> <br /> Also, weather eye and how it abreviates journeys means a wraith finds a byway? Is that how you see the power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T10:47:45-08:00","id":399011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/391536-playtesting-wraith-20-argos?p=395899#post395899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one turn per success rule has always been part of Phantom Wings ...</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my recollection as well. I've not seen the new writeup -- is it public or is it a specific KS reward? Does it still say you must be incorporeal? I always thought that bit was a little mysterious, logically tacking on a corpus point cost (unless you already happen to have been disrupted for some other reason, of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4448-bphillips","name":"bphillips","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T12:19:18-08:00","id":399169,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">I interpret Weather Eye (Argo One, Modern) as an &quot;ad hoc byway&quot; power. The Harbinger, aware of its nuances and fluctuations, figures out a way through the Tempest. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">A RL analogy:</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Someone is wilderness hiking.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\">They see an established path and follow it (a byway).</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Another hiker decides that paths are for pansies and wanders into the forest/desert (Traveling in the Tempest unaided).</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">The third hiker, more savvy than the first two, doesn't use the path. Nor does he blindly traipse about the wilderness. Instead, he sees areas where the growth isn't that bad, places where the rocks look stable, etc. He's not using the path, but he's using his expertise to make an ad hoc path (Harbinger). </span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">That's kinda how I see it. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">YMMV.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T13:07:12-08:00","id":399208,"title":"","content":"What I personally might need help with is describing Tempest Travel beyond A ROLLING STORM OF NOTHINGNESS AND EMOTIONS!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T09:28:39-08:00","id":401966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But in actual play i've been feeling that travel is a very big narrative concern for wraith games. It is very difficult. </div> </div> </div>This is on purpose. There are very few myths about Ghost that travel apart from those bound into moving Haunts, ghost trains, ships etc. Hence traveling is hard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A wraith needs to travel through the tempest, not always safe, or walk very long distances. </div> </div> </div>True, but like I mentioned above on purpose, yet there still multiple ways around both restrictions through Arcanoi. Puppetry allows one to hitch a ride inside someone and thus use any mode of transportation available for them, Inhabit allows for you to possess vehicles or just surge through the electric highway while Lifeweb provides fast travel to your Fetters etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've not seen the new writeup -- is it public or is it a specific KS reward? </div> </div> </div>It's public and a link to it, and a few others, can be found in the Wr20 Kickstarter page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T13:14:59-08:00","id":404994,"title":"","content":"Okay, another series of questions regarding Argos.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> When a Wraith creates a Nihil to enter the Tempest, or uses an existing one, where in the Tempest does he go? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Is it the open sea, from where Nihils are seen as stars above? Or necessarily on, or near, a byway that leads through the Necropolis where the wraith entered the Tempest? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Since someone approaching that Necropolis through the Tempest would be using that byway, i suppose byways near Necropolis are &quot;fixed&quot; landmarks. Or are they? At least tempest portals are, right?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I suppose existing nihils lead to the open sea, since this is where they are seen. This means that if i open a nihil near an existing natural occurring one i will arrive in the tempest near to where the natural nihil leads, or not necessarily?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Can the wraith use weather eye to find a safe pathway before opening the nihil, or only after entering the tempest?<br /> <br /> What do you guys think or use on your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T19:51:43-08:00","id":406304,"title":"","content":"One thing that is a slight annoyance is that to get the opening Nihils with these new rules is that a player will have to buy both ancient and modern. So, if not access to the Ancient Art form than the player will have to use naturally occurnig Nihils or The Instant-Nihil Artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T08:39:05-07:00","id":445968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/391536-playtesting-wraith-20-argos?p=401966#post401966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is on purpose. There are very few myths about Ghost that travel apart from those bound into moving Haunts, ghost trains, ships etc. Hence traveling is hard.<br /> <br /> <br /> True, but like I mentioned above on purpose, yet there still multiple ways around both restrictions through Arcanoi. Puppetry allows one to hitch a ride inside someone and thus use any mode of transportation available for them, Inhabit allows for you to possess vehicles or just surge through the electric highway while Lifeweb provides fast travel to your Fetters etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's public and a link to it, and a few others, can be found in the Wr20 Kickstarter page.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the Midnight Express, which is good for getting around (and has edible food!).<br /> <br /> The new rules for Weather Eye (level one) are helpful for Shadowlands travel. I also like that the basic powers are folded into the level one arts. It's not really until level four, however, that you can travel at any speed to destinations in the Tempest (the lower-level arts indicate 'nearby' locations). But that seems to make sense, as travel through the Tempest should be tricky.<br /> <br /> In general, I think the new Argos is much better balanced the old one, so many of the mobility issues will be lessened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T14:42:24-07:00","id":446548,"title":"","content":"I'm a Wraith20 backer, but I must have missed this. Where was a new Argos made available?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T17:12:40-07:00","id":446742,"title":"","content":"Go to the Kickstarter page and scroll down. Looks like it's about 1/4 of the way, A set of mostly Dropbox links.<br /> <br /> Chapter 1, Usury, Inhabit, Argos and Lifeweb drafts are all available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T23:19:52-07:00","id":447205,"title":"","content":"Awesome! Thanks! Kinda bummed to see Basic Techniques disappear, though. I liked those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T08:28:46-07:00","id":447729,"title":"","content":"Glad to be of service.<br /> <br /> Me too. Except for Phantasm. That was pretty lame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T08:52:59-07:00","id":451576,"title":"","content":"How are you that are trying out the new Argos Arcanoi feeling about the pushing of Basic Abilities into Early Dots of the power?<br /> The Argos player in my group is, at the moment, not so keen on having to buy two powers from different branches to just accomplish what is character can currently do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T18:38:12-07:00","id":457567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mental-Mouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/391536-playtesting-wraith-20-argos?p=451576#post451576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are you that are trying out the new Argos Arcanoi feeling about the pushing of Basic Abilities into Early Dots of the power?<br /> The Argos player in my group is, at the moment, not so keen on having to buy two powers from different branches to just accomplish what is character can currently do.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more elegant but less versatile. I liked Basic Abilities, because it allowed people to purchase very low-powered but useful advantages very cheaply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T19:32:06-07:00","id":459602,"title":"","content":"Yes, I shall mourn Basic Abilities. Though maybe there is still time to Salvage them!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T16:57:09-07:00","id":461649,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I liked how they became part of the first dot at first (it simplifies things), but I miss them now.<br /> <br /> Oh, and my house rule is probably going to address the 'low power' critique earlier in the thread: I'm going to allow five successes or more to allow travel for a full scene, rather than simply one turn per success. It seems that three successes or more should have a better outcome than just a few more seconds of flight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T11:58:38-07:00","id":463702,"title":"","content":"Being on how hard it would to be to make it work, Imma thinking that I'll just use modified older version of Arcanoi than the new ones as Basic Abilities really have just worked so much better for me in my game. Haven't tried to other ones yet but the Argos player just gave up on the new ones and moved back to using he ones printed in the 2e book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T12:43:42-07:00","id":463731,"title":"","content":"I like the fact that the new way is more consistent with the rest of the entire WoD. You could always just house-rule that 1-dot arts are cheaper than list price, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4448-bphillips","name":"bphillips","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T15:04:29-07:00","id":463918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mental-Mouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/391536-playtesting-wraith-20-argos?p=463702#post463702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being on how hard it would to be to make it work, Imma thinking that I'll just use modified older version of Arcanoi than the new ones as Basic Abilities really have just worked so much better for me in my game. Haven't tried to other ones yet but the Argos player just gave up on the new ones and moved back to using he ones printed in the 2e book.</div> </div> </div> </div>How did you handle basic abilities? A Wraith is considered to have the first dot of an Arcanos after learning them? Is the first dot a requisite to learning basic abilities? Or they exist independently of Arcanoi mastery? Also, these would be house rules, no? It is my understanding that no wraith book ever touched the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T17:11:02-07:00","id":465353,"title":"","content":"As of now, which is still a work in progress, a Character creation, any Arcanoi you buy the 1st Do y of comes with all the basic abilities.<br /> Post-Creation you have to buy the basic abilities up before taking the 1st dot. It works well enough for most but the Likes of Argos, which has a higher than average number of 'em, takes a lot more to get the 1st dot of.<br /> <br /> I consider Basic abilities the fundamentals you gotta learn before taking the 1st Dot.<br /> Like Needing to know Basic Math before going onto Higher Maths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T02:59:19-07:00","id":465853,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you can buy a Basic Ability with XP without getting the first dot. It allows characters to have a wide range of basic powers without spending huge amounts of XP. I always liked that, as it encourages a diverse range of traits without characters suddenly having to become experts in an unlikely range of Arcanoi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T16:35:52-07:00","id":466638,"title":"","content":"Yar the loss of the Basic Abilities is really a poor choice In my opinion.<br /> It twas like a tasty buffet O' little snacks you could take. Useful but not overly so over a full Arancoi ability.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T20:25:49-07:00","id":469811,"title":"","content":"Well I played a WtO game tonight, and we playtested the new Argos rules. What struck me was how difficult movement was in the game, and how that really makes a difference to pace, crucially. Every time a wraith wants to travel, they have to plan a lot, and you either have to skip over big chunks of time or roleplay lots of the logistics (which isn't fun in my real life, let alone in a roleplaying game).<br /> <br /> There are wide stretches of land (particularly in the USA) where wraiths would be exposed to maelstroms and spectres. The pace would slow to a crawl as soon as any wraith left a necropolis, because they can no longer rely on the Midnight Express. Even crossing bodies of water is painfully slow without a relic craft. (Although I was very pleased that I managed to improvise a raft and use Phantom Wings as rudders to help steer the craft to shore.)<br /> <br /> I think, as a house rule, five successes on a Phantom Wings roll should be enough to allow its use for an entire scene. After all, it's still at normal walking (up to jogging) speed, so you really can't get very far. Crossing a 400m body of water would require 16 turns, if we assume speed of 25m/turn. Even as an extended roll, that's a lot of successes. Allowing Phantom Wings for a scene, but with Dexterity-based rolls whenever obstacles occur or whenever a character needs to manoeuvre/change directions, would be much better. Five successes is usually considered an exceptional result anyway.<br /> <br /> Any more thoughts on this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":".  Corrected bad maths due to exhaustion. 04-06-2015, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T23:29:57-07:00","id":469912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even crossing bodies of water is painfully slow without a relic craft. </div> </div> </div>How so? It is usually faster for Wraith than it is for humans without a relic craft as Wraiths may just walk/jog/run on the the water.<br /> <br /> Also I have to repeat myself a bit here but traveling long distances isn't really a ghostly thing in myths or anywhere aside from following their Fetters, that is haunting people or vehicles. And when travel is needed Argos facilitates that through the Tempest and is pretty much the only means to travel to the Dark Kingdoms within, also it is the nature of the Tempest to defy time and distance which makes travel faster, and Argos helps with this too though not through granting flight and it does so at level 1 on the new version which also tends to guarantee safe travel. But like I said there are other methods of travelling as well, methods much more in theme with ghost than growing wings and flying to places like possessing computers and travelling through the Electric Highway, Possessing a human and traveling that way, just short cutting directly to that Fetter of yours that moved away through Lifeweb, possessing actual vehicles and moving like that or just plain not using any Arcanoi and walking into a plane or a train along with the living passengers.<br /> <br /> Wraiths do not actually need sustained flight to facilitate movement and they require far less preparation and logistics than humans when travelling, or Vampires for example.<br /> <br /> Sure you can extend Phantom Wings to last a scene, and in that regards the rule of it requiring 5 successes on the activation roll is a pretty nice ruling, but I still fail to see the need for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T06:19:26-07:00","id":470086,"title":"","content":"See, the 'water as solid' thing was never clear to me. I know there was something in Blood-Dimmed Tides, but I never read that book. Even if a wraith could walk through the water, wouldn't they pass through the surface and wind up on the waterbed? So either at the bottom of a sea or river, which would mean climbing out again. I'm not sure why water would be otherwise as solid as concrete for a wraith.<br /> <br /> I also disagree that all ghost stories have ghosts as immobile. There are myths and legends about flying hordes of the dead, and in popular culture there are plenty of representations of hovering and floating ghosts. <br /> <br /> But, more importantly, Wraith has a really vast universe, and a really treacherous one. There are enough obstacles already that a lack of travel just makes the game that much harder (and where time is limited, it eats into time that could otherwise be used for more rewarding roleplaying experiences). The alternative is that many wraiths would quickly learn one of the Arcanoi arts to travel. Especially wraiths used to the relative independence and freedom of having had a car in their mortal life. Many people drive to the corner shop now. Cultures where car use is prevalent would see more wraiths coming up with their own independent methods of travel that don't rely on the Quick or Hierarchy.<br /> <br /> But I'll admit bias here, because I get serious commuter rage. The last thing I want when I want to get somewhere is to be travelling on someone else's schedule and surrounded by strangers.<br /> <br /> I guess if it's really just me that feels this way, though, it's not the end of the world if I just house rule it. I only brought it up because others have pointed out similar house rules, and if we're playtesting stuff we should share our worries and concerns.<br /> <br /> Alternatively (and this may be something that pleases everybody), maybe there can be a sidebar somewhere in Wraith 20th that offers some suggestions for non-Arcanos means of travel that are likely to be available? I feel like that information could be really useful for players and Storytellers alike (especially because the universe of Wraith requires the biggest learning curve for people to imagine out of all the cWoD games).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T08:10:13-07:00","id":470156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See, the 'water as solid' thing was never clear to me. I know there was something in Blood-Dimmed Tides, but I never read that book. Even if a wraith could walk through the water, wouldn't they pass through the surface and wind up on the waterbed? So either at the bottom of a sea or river, which would mean climbing out again. I'm not sure why water would be otherwise as solid as concrete for a wraith. </div> </div> </div>Well according to the Blood-Dimmed Tides water is solid as a rock to the Dead, unless you drowned in which case you have a merit that allows you to swim for longer periods per Corpus level, so no you wouldn't end up in the river bed but rather cross it safely. Also Argos level one, Weather Eye (Modern) in Wraith20, allows for faster and safer mode of transit than Phantom Wings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also disagree that all ghost stories have ghosts as immobile. There are myths and legends about flying hordes of the dead, and in popular culture there are plenty of representations of hovering and floating ghosts. </div> </div> </div>Most of these do not fly around long distances but rather hoover in place or around the place they haunt. That is their mobility is often tied to either their Fetter, Haunt or a Relic in Wraith terms. But considering the staggering amount of ghost stories out there I admit there might be a few where the ghost fly on ghostly wings but these are usually exceptions not the rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, more importantly, Wraith has a really vast universe, and a really treacherous one. There are enough obstacles already that a lack of travel just makes the game that much harder (and where time is limited, it eats into time that could otherwise be used for more rewarding roleplaying experiences). The alternative is that many wraiths would quickly learn one of the Arcanoi arts to travel. Especially wraiths used to the relative independence and freedom of having had a car in their mortal life. Many people drive to the corner shop now. Cultures where car use is prevalent would see more wraiths coming up with their own independent methods of travel that don't rely on the Quick or Hierarchy. </div> </div> </div>Yes it's a dangerous world out there, and vast, but that is why Argos level 1 helps by allowing you to use Tempest shortcuts to cut down the travel time considerably and even make it a safer journey. Seriously this one low level power is amazing.<br /> But all Arcanoi aside Wraiths can always just catch a ride on any Skinlands vehicle that passes them, if someone else is boarding as well it's completely free otherwise it cost you a Corpus level to jump through the door. Aside from that there is the possibility of Relic vehicles, in which case the Argos 1 power can still help make it even faster and like said safer. All in all Wraiths still have easier time to travel than Vampires for instance their greatest problem while traveling is that they end up far from their Fetters, and this is where Lifeweb comes in handy, and should they face adversity may find themselves back at their Fetter after a Harrowing.<br /> <br /> I've never seen this to be that problematic of an issue. You need to travel a longer distance as fast as possible? Hop a plane heading to that direction and your golden. No Arcanoi needed though Puppetry 1 Skinride makes this a more pleasant experience, as you get to enjoy inflight meal and other small pleasures of the living while traveling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T08:50:16-07:00","id":470174,"title":"","content":"Water is weirdly hard and soft to Wraiths. Kinda like French Onion soup. There's something hard and crunchy and <i>moving </i>on top, underneath it's just like any other liquid to swim in, you just can't really hold your breath and have to bob up (or pop out?) VERY often. It's hard unless they spend 1 Corpus and go Incorporeal. Then they can swim just like anyone else for turns = Sta. If they can't surface at the end, the lose another Corpus and get Sta more turns. So wraiths can &quot;drown&quot; pretty easily and messily, considering the consequences of 0 Corpus. The Drowned Merit comes in 3-6 pt versions, with the intervals for Corpus loss going up significantly, from 6 hours all the way to &quot;never&quot;.<br /> <br /> Wraiths have hard &quot;lives&quot;. Travel isn't easy, but it seems slightly less dangerous than for a vampire and there are a number of options as previously mentioned: Argos, Inhabit (&quot;stowing away&quot;?), Puppetry (&quot;hitch-hiking&quot;?) or just taking your chances and walking, riding a Relic, etc. from here to there. Which is probably the MOST dangerous way to do it, particularly in the wider spaces between settlements and the farther West you go in America (the remnants of the Dark Lands of Flint like to pick off travelers...). If you are pathological about having to be in control of your own travel (which you never really are unless you are off-roading though some wide-open space), you should invest in Argos and brave the Tempest or get a Relic vehicle and brave the emptiness of the Underworld where there are no convenient Haunts, etc.<br /> <br /> There might be a fair number of Relic water craft. People seem to invest heavily emotionally in their boats and boats sink, rot, etc. pretty often. You'll probably need to make a deal with someone with the Drowned Merit to do the recovery work, but then you can go anywhere the craft would normally. Which means you lose certain values of control; similar to what you lose when you have to, say, drive on roads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 04-06-2015, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T10:32:37-07:00","id":470241,"title":"","content":"Those last two posts were a great help and, I think, are exactly the kind of setting info that should be included in either the core book or Storyteller's Screen when Wr20 comes out. It helps to conceptualise things a lot more, which was always a problem with new players to Wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}